<article class="env-lemma" id="0AP2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AP2">Lemma <span data-tag="0AP2">15.45.4</span>.</a> If $A \to B$ is an étale ring map and $A$ is a Dedekind domain, then $B$ is a finite product of Dedekind domains. In particular, the localizations $B_\mathfrak q$ for $\mathfrak q \subset B$ maximal are discrete valuation rings. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement on the local rings follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/07QP" data-tag="07QP">15.45.2</a> and <a href="/tag/0AH0" data-tag="0AH0">15.45.3</a> and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00PD" data-tag="00PD">10.119.7</a>. It follows that $B$ is a Noetherian normal ring of dimension $1$. By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/030C" data-tag="030C">10.37.16</a> we conclude that $B$ is a finite product of normal domains of dimension $1$. These are Dedekind domains by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/034X" data-tag="034X">10.120.17</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>